{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 25,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These are additional proverbs of Solomon, which were copied by the men of Hezekiah king of Judah:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is the glory of God to conceal a matter and the glory of kings to search it out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As the heavens are high and the earth is deep, so the hearts of kings cannot be searched.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remove the dross from the silver, and a vessel for a silversmith will come forth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remove the wicked from the king’s presence, and his throne will be established in righteousness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not exalt yourself in the presence of the king, and do not stand in the place of great men;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "for it is better to be told, “Come up here!” than to be demoted in the presence of the prince. Even what you have seen with your own eyes,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "do not bring hastily to court. Otherwise, what will you do in the end when your neighbor puts you to shame?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Argue your case with your neighbor without betraying another’s confidence,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "lest he who hears you bring shame upon you, and your infamy never go away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A word fitly spoken is like apples of gold in settings of silver.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Like an earring of gold or an ornament of fine gold is a wise man’s rebuke to a listening ear.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Like the cold of snow in the time of harvest is a trustworthy messenger to those who send him; he refreshes the soul of his masters.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Like clouds and wind without rain is the man who boasts of gifts never given.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Through patience a ruler can be persuaded, and a gentle tongue can break a bone.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If you find honey, eat just what you need, lest you have too much and vomit it up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Seldom set foot in your neighbor’s house, lest he grow weary and hate you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Like a club or sword or sharp arrow is a man who bears false witness against his neighbor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Like a broken tooth or a foot out of joint is confidence in a faithless man in time of trouble.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Like one who removes a garment on a cold day or vinegar poured on a wound is one who sings songs to a heavy heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If your enemy is hungry, give him food to eat, and if he is thirsty, give him water to drink.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For in so doing, you will heap burning coals on his head, and the LORD will reward you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As the north wind brings forth rain, so a backbiting tongue brings angry looks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Better to live on a corner of the roof than to share a house with a quarrelsome wife.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Like cold water to a weary soul is good news from a distant land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Like a muddied spring or a polluted well is a righteous man who gives way to the wicked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is not good to eat too much honey or to search out one’s own glory.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.25.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Like a city whose walls are broken down is a man who does not control his temper.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
